						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1047.msg10477#msg10477"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1047.msg10477#msg10477">Re: Omens of War - Will you Buy it?</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #20 on:</b> August 26, 2004, 12:30:14 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I&#039;m really pissed about the druid rez bullshit. I&#039;ll likely not buy the expansion soley due to this. Perhaps when class balance happens on a realistic scale I may reconsider. Until then I&#039;ll not be participating in pumping out more&nbsp; super unbalanced classes, while others are in dire need of a real work over. Sony(Adolf) can keep their super-children, I want no part or proximity of it.<br /><br />Admitedly, Sony is aware of the balancing issue, but would rather pump out revenue, then actually fix broken content, classes, and game design before hand. This backburner approach is a little too much to stomach much more.<br /><br />Although my post may reflect my attitude, I will leave my vote blank for now.
						</td>
					</tr>
